  "solution": {
    "approach": "Use nested loops to iterate through rows and columns, printing characters corresponding to the pattern formula.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(N^2)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(N^2)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() { int n; if(scanf(\"%d\",&n)==1){for(int i=1;i<=n;i++){for(int j=0;j<i;j++)putchar('a'+i-1);putchar('\\n');}}return 0; }",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){int n;if(cin>>n){for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)cout<<string(i,(char)('a'+i-1))<<\"\\n\";}return 0;}",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main{public static void main(String[] args){Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);if(sc.hasNextInt()){int n=sc.nextInt();for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)System.out.println(String.valueOf((char)('a'+i-1)).repeat(i));}}}",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndef pattern(n):\n    return '\\n'.join(chr(97 + i - 1) * i for i in range(1, n + 1))\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    if s:\n        print(pattern(int(s)))\nmain()",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\nconst s = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();\nif (s) { const n = parseInt(s, 10); for(let i=1;i<=n;i++)console.log(String.fromCharCode(97+i-1).repeat(i));}"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Print the required pattern line-by-line using nested loops based on line index and character offset."
